<!--
  RM_SandBusters.xml                      RimMandrake — SANDBUSTER_CASTES_BUILD_1

  The two sand-buster castes, ruled at NIGHTSIDE_ICE_DESIGN_SITTING_1 (2026-09-24
  amendment to dune_sea.md) and named/scoped at STILLSAND_DESIGN_SITTING_1
  (2026-09-27, Q9/Q14). Both coins checker 6/6 and Wookieepedia 0-hit (probed
  live 2026-09-27) — confirmed non-canon, RM_-tier per Q11a, per the item's own
  provenance note; not re-checked here.

  These two PawnKindDefs are ONLY ever spawned by RM_SandBusterMound's own
  CompProperties_SpawnerPawn (see RM_SandBusterMound.xml) — neither is wired
  into RM_Stillsand_Biome.xml's <wildAnimals>. That is deliberate, not an
  oversight: dune_sea.md §4 makes the whole biome event-driven ("the default
  state of the dune sea is dormancy... it wakes up because something did
  something"), and vanilla's own Megaspider/Spelopede/Megascarab are handled
  the same way — threat-spawned by Hive, never a roster animal. Adding
  these to wildAnimals would also violate the item's own "do not add
  anything beyond the two ruled castes + mound + incident" constraint by
  turning an event-driven ambush threat into an ambient population.

  §6's bimodal law ("giant or grain-scale, nothing between... a hard gap
  where every ordinary animal would be") is why there are TWO castes here
  where vanilla's Hive has THREE (Megascarab/Spelopede/Megaspider): the
  biome's own hard ban on medium bodies (R22's 0.3-3.0 mid-band) collapses
  vanilla's small/medium/large trio onto exactly the two poles the sheet
  allows. Ruukka is the giant pole, oorrik is the grain pole; there is no
  "medium sand buster" and there is not supposed to be one.

  SILHOUETTE (the sheet's own worst-offence clause, §6/Amendment: "no
  recognisable spider/insect silhouette... a nameable giant is this sheet's
  worst offence"): a RimWorld race's visual silhouette is entirely its ART
  (texPath), never its BodyDef — BodyDef governs the health/hitbox skeleton
  only (RimSage-confirmed: Hive's own spawnablePawnKinds read
  Props.spawnablePawnKinds per-instance, nothing about body shape). So
  neither caste below uses an insectoid BodyDef (BeetleLike/
  BeetleLikeWithClaw, vanilla Megascarab/Megaspider's own bodies) — both use
  plain mammalian quadruped skeletons, functionally identical to half this
  biome's existing predator roster (RM_Vekka, RM_Drazzik). The actual "does
  not read as a spider/beetle" requirement is carried by the ART BRIEF (see
  each PawnKindDef's texPath comment and the artpipe job filed for this
  item) — reusing a non-insect functional skeleton is necessary but not
  sufficient, and whoever renders these must draw an eruption-adapted
  burrower/driller silhouette, not a bug with a new paint job.

  SUN-AXIS POLARISATION (§4: "every organism is polarised on the sun-axis...
  the sun-face is mirror, ceramic, ablative armour... the shade-face carries
  every opening the organism has"): both castes spend almost their entire
  life below the sand and only briefly present a sun-face when they erupt
  to strike — so the asymmetry is described in-fiction (dorsal plate vs.
  soft ventral maw/digging face) and reflected mechanically the same way
  RM_Oommok's is: through stats (heavy armor, nothing about a split
  BodyDef) rather than a second body. This mirrors this mod's own existing
  precedent (RM_Oommok's header: "that asymmetry is a property of the ART...
  not something a BodyDef could express").

  STATS: both castes use surpriseAttack stun bonuses on their first strike,
  matching this biome's established "erupts and strikes before you can
  react" pattern (RM_Vekka, RM_Drazzik — same mechanic, same precedent).
  combatPower values are set so a mound's CompProperties_SpawnerPawn
  (initialPawnsPoints 200 / maxSpawnedPawnsPoints 500, unchanged from
  vanilla Hive) produces "one or two giants plus a real grain-scale swarm"
  rather than either pole alone.

  ART: no render exists for "ruukka"/"sand buster"/"oorrik" anywhere in
  infrastructure/artpipe/{done,pending,_artsrc}/registry.jsonl (checked this
  pass). Two 3-facing jobs filed (infrastructure/artpipe/art_lists/
  sandbuster_castes.csv -> pending/RM_Ruukka_{south,east,north}.json,
  RM_Oorrik_{south,east,north}.json) — both prompts
  explicitly require the no-insect-silhouette + sun-face/shade-face split;
  texPaths below point at each def's own future folder, art pending, same
  posture this mod's other unrendered ports use (RM_Ikee, RM_Vekka,
  RM_Drazzik, RM_Aurrok).
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- ============== Ruukka — the giant eruptor ============== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Ruukka</defName>
    <label>ruukka</label>
    <description>A driving wedge of plate and muscle that spends its entire life a metre under the dune crest, and only ever shows itself once: coming straight up through the sand, dorsal plate first, in the half-second before it hits something. What surfaces is armoured top to bottom in fused, sun-bright scale; what it turns toward its prey afterward, jaws and digging claws both, has never once seen the light before that moment. It does not chase. It does not need to.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>2.6</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>1400</Mass>
      <MarketValue>0</MarketValue>
      <Wildness>1.0</Wildness>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>100</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>1.0</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.6</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>2.0</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <PainShockThreshold>0.8</PainShockThreshold>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <FilthRate>4</FilthRate>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>left drill-claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
          <li>Stab</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>22</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.8</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <surpriseAttack>
          <extraMeleeDamages>
            <li>
              <def>Stun</def>
              <amount>32</amount>
            </li>
          </extraMeleeDamages>
        </surpriseAttack>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>right drill-claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
          <li>Stab</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>22</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.8</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontRightPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <surpriseAttack>
          <extraMeleeDamages>
            <li>
              <def>Stun</def>
              <amount>32</amount>
            </li>
          </extraMeleeDamages>
        </surpriseAttack>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>jaws</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>24</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.0</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <surpriseAttack>
          <extraMeleeDamages>
            <li>
              <def>Stun</def>
              <amount>26</amount>
            </li>
          </extraMeleeDamages>
        </surpriseAttack>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>plated head</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>14</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.2</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail</body>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <predator>true</predator>
      <!-- Giant pole of §6's bimodal law (bs >=4, this mod's Q8-ratified floor). -->
      <baseBodySize>5.0</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>6.0</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.0</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>OmnivoreAnimal</foodType>
      <leatherDef>Leather_Heavy</leatherDef>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <petness>0</petness>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <gestationPeriodDays>0</gestationPeriodDays>
      <lifeExpectancy>6</lifeExpectancy>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalFighter</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Ruukka</defName>
    <label>ruukka</label>
    <labelPlural>ruukkas</labelPlural>
    <race>RM_Ruukka</race>
    <!-- Never wild-spawned (not in any biome's wildAnimals — see this file's
         header); faction is forced to the spawning mound's own faction
         (Faction.OfInsects) by CompSpawnerPawn.TrySpawnPawn regardless of
         this field, but set for the same documentary reason vanilla's own
         InsectKindBase sets it. -->
    <defaultFactionDef>Insect</defaultFactionDef>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <combatPower>230</combatPower>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <!-- art pending — SANDBUSTER_CASTES_BUILD_1, pending/RM_Ruukka_{south,
               east,north}.json filed. Brief:
               NO insect/spider silhouette; dorsal sun-face plate vs. soft
               ventral shade-face split must read clearly. -->
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Ruukka/RM_Ruukka</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>3.2</drawSize>
          <shadowData>
            <volume>(0.5, 0.6, 0.45)</volume>
            <offset>(0,0,-0.1)</offset>
          </shadowData>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!-- ============== Oorrik — the grain swarm ============== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Oorrik</defName>
    <label>oorrik</label>
    <description>A single oorrik is nothing — a wet-mouthed sliver of a thing barely bigger than the grains it moves through. A mound's worth of them is a different problem: dozens surfacing in the same half-second across ten metres of sand, each one too small to hit and too many to count. Nothing about any one of them is dangerous. That was never the point.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>5.5</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>0.3</Mass>
      <MarketValue>0</MarketValue>
      <Wildness>1.0</Wildness>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>100</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <MeatAmount>0</MeatAmount>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>mouthparts</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>7</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.4</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>foreclaw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>5</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>Rat</body>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <predator>true</predator>
      <!-- Grain pole of §6's bimodal law (matches this mod's own ikee at 0.15). -->
      <baseBodySize>0.18</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.3</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.0</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>OmnivoreAnimal</foodType>
      <leatherDef>Leather_Light</leatherDef>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <petness>0</petness>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <gestationPeriodDays>0</gestationPeriodDays>
      <lifeExpectancy>2</lifeExpectancy>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalFighter</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Oorrik</defName>
    <label>oorrik</label>
    <labelPlural>oorriks</labelPlural>
    <race>RM_Oorrik</race>
    <defaultFactionDef>Insect</defaultFactionDef>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <!-- Low per-unit combatPower is deliberate — against a mound's fixed
         initialPawnsPoints/maxSpawnedPawnsPoints (200/500, unchanged from
         vanilla Hive) a low figure here is what makes "grain swarm" true in
         play: many oorrik spawn per points budget rather than one or two. -->
    <combatPower>16</combatPower>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <!-- art pending — SANDBUSTER_CASTES_BUILD_1, pending/RM_Oorrik_{south,
               east,north}.json filed. Brief:
               NO insect/spider silhouette; grain-scale, not a scaled-down
               copy of ruukka's art. -->
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Oorrik/RM_Oorrik</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.55</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
